# Captain dev workflow (Prakrit)

This is **Prakrit's** (captain) process. Full copy:
[`docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md).

When the user is **Akhil**, follow [`docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md)
instead: do not open a studio plan or file Linear tickets unless he asks.

Read **`docs/agents/captain-dev-workflow.md`**, **`docs/agents/agent-tooling-index.md`**, and
**`docs/share/proplane-collaborator-workflow.md`** (for sharing with friends).

**① Plan (studio) → ② Iterate until `approved` → ③ Execute → ④ Review → ⑤ Promote**

## ① Plan, ② iterate (default)

If the captain describes work, a bug, an idea, or pastes feedback — write this
lane's plan in the **PropLane studio** before anything else, even if he did not
ask.

```bash
node ~/proplane-mock-kit/tools/studio-plan.mjs new --lane <lane> --id <id> --title "<title>"
```

**Do not file a Linear ticket for it.** The plan is the artifact; file a ticket
only when he explicitly asks.

The scaffold is a shell — fill it. The UI tab must **mock the screen** in
PropLane tokens (before/after, desktop/mobile, empty + loading + error), and the
plan stays editable and semi-interactive so he can rewrite it in place. Standard:
**`docs/agents/lavish-plan-standard.md`**. Gate: **`lavish-plan-gate.mdc`**.

Reply with the lane's studio URL + what the plan proposes. **Stop until the
plan is buildable** — `studio-plan.mjs status --lane <lane>` exits 0 once its
status is `approved`, `built`, or `skipped`.

Skip only when he says **`skip plan`** (hotfix).

Watch: `node ~/proplane-mock-kit/tools/studio-inbox.mjs --lane <lane> --wait`
as a tracked background task — the plan's chat and annotations reach you
through it and nowhere else, so never end a turn with a plan open and no
watcher running. Reply inside the studio, where he wrote the note.

UI work: follow `docs/agents/ui-change-checklist.md`

## ③ Execute

- Lane branch + sandbox port: this pane's own local instructions
  (gitignored `.cursor/rules/local-agent-branch.mdc`), never hard-coded in the repo.
- Read `docs/portal-ui-system.md` before portal UI; `docs/agents/<area>.md` before features.
- MCP: `.cursor/mcp.json` — see agent-tooling-index.
- Build **what the plan shows**. A departure means updating `plan.html` and saying so.

## ④ Review

Test on **this pane's sandbox URL**. After UI/route fixes run `npm run sandbox:open -- </route>` so the captain lands on the feature instantly (`sandbox-open-feature-review.mdc`). Do not merge to `prakrit`, `main`, `staging`, or `production` yourself.

Only touch Linear when he asked for a ticket: comment the SHA with
`npm run linear:comment`, and never move a peer-verified Done issue back to Backlog.

## ⑤ Promote (captain only)

Type in the lane's pane (or prakrit pane for later rungs):

```bash
/promote prakrit                  # fold keeper → prakrit (no-mistakes)
/promote main                     # prakrit → main
/promote staging                  # main → staging (QA)
/promote staging to production    # staging → production (live + TestFlight)
```

## Production data

Default routine work to dev/test Supabase. Production changes require explicit
authorization for the exact scope plus a reviewed, backed-up, fail-closed apply
path and post-apply verification. The separate live-listing lock still applies.
